  "content_en": "The concubine seeks to marry the best princess: \"Girl, please sleep a little longer, it's only three o'clock!\" \"No, Qingxing, I'd better get up!\" Ninth Sister hugged the fragrant and warm cup again, and then she no longer lingered and sat up resolutely. According to the time in the previous life, it was still less than six o'clock, which was indeed very early. But she would get up at this time every day, for no other reason than to strive to be a well-behaved young lady in the prince's mansion, in order to live a peaceful and stable life. After cleaning up, I ate a simple breakfast as usual, and then went out to pay my respects to the third lady, accompanied by Qingxing Qingtao. There was a strong westerly wind all night, and the weather was indeed a bit cold. Sister Jiu couldn't help but wrap her old cloak around her body. She looked at the one or two stars still dotting the sky and sighed softly in her heart. Just hang in there, things will get better gradually! No? Doesn’t she already have her own independent residence, so she no longer has to share the two cabins with her aunt? Didn't she already use nutrition and exercise to make her body, which used to take two steps and gasp twice, very healthy? Hasn't she already trained her own maid, so she no longer has to be controlled by others in everything? Hasn’t she already obtained all of Master Su’s true inheritance, so she won’t go hungry no matter how things change in the future? Looking up again at the twinkling stars in the sky, Sister Wenjiu couldn't help but slowly reveal a smile on her pretty face. \"Miss Ninth, you are still on time. Come in and warm yourself up. My wife has just gotten up and is cleaning up.\" When they arrived at the third lady's place, the beautiful maid Cui Qiao, wearing a green collar with pink and blue flowers and a waist-to-breasted waistband, came out to welcome her and raised the curtain for her. \"Thank you Sister Cuiqiao!\" Sister Jiu said her thanks with a smile and entered the house. Taking a deep breath of the warm air that hit her face, Jiu Jie'er worked on the round cake that Cuiqiao brought over, while listening to the movement in the west room, which was the living room of the third lady. \"Mother Zhou and Cuimei are serving Madam's breakfast. Aunt Xu came over just now, but Madam asked her to go back first, saying that she is recovering from illness and will take good care of herself before coming back to serve her.\" Cui Qiao stood by the brazier, adding silver bone charcoal to it quickly, and turned to look at her and said. Sister Jiu was startled, then smiled, and took out a handkerchief from her sleeve, \"By the way, Sister Cuiqiao, I suddenly remembered that I brought you the handkerchief you said you dropped at my place a few days ago. Take a look... is it right?\" This piece?\" Cuiqiao was startled, her eyes quickly passing over the handkerchief embroidered with flowers and birds, and then a look of surprise appeared on her face, \"That's it, Miss Jiu!\" \"Put it away quickly, don't drop it again.\" Sister Wenjiu smiled at her. Cuiqiao quickly stuffed the handkerchief into her arms, smiled back at Sister Jiu, and hurriedly poured her tea. Looking at her Pingting's back, a hint of cunning flashed through Sister Wenjiu's bright eyes. Of course this veil is not Cui Qiao's, but it is not embroidered by Master Su as Cui Qiao hoped. Master Su from Jinxiu Pavilion is the most famous embroidery master in Bianzhong City. An ordinary piece of embroidery work can cost a fortune. Fortunately, such an expert became the embroidery master of the Wen family girls because of his close relationship with the old lady. Of course, the happiest people are the maids and ladies of the Wen family, the wealthy and wealthy ladies. Whoever relies on craftsmanship in the future will only learn one more skill, and it is they who require strong technical skills. I originally thought that by virtue of being close to the water, I could get some advice from Master Su, but after trying it, I realized that this was simply a luxury. So many people began to settle for the next best thing, changing their grand goal to getting Master Su's embroidery samples to study and figure out. But this seems difficult... In fact, only Sister Wenjiu and a few people understand that unless the loss is accidental and unplanned, it is unlikely. Let alone how eccentric Master Su's temperament is and how serious her thoughts are, we can tell from the fact that every piece of her embroidery will be collected with a lot of money. However, this is not a problem for Sister Wenjiu. It is just a question of whether she is willing or not, because she can imitate Master Su's embroidery very closely, to the extent that it is fake and real, and even non-professionals will not be able to tell the difference. Of course, how much hard work and effort she put into this was only known to her. In the first year of her arrival in this other world, she spent almost all her time and effort on this embroidery. Fortunately, she loved crafts in her previous life, and by chance, she fell into the eyes of the eccentric and aloof Master Su. Master Su not only accepted her as a closed disciple, but also took the initiative to help her cover up the world.She was so clumsy that she finally mastered a skill in this other world. Only in this way could she feel calm and at ease in her heart. She had no choice but to be self-reliant, and she longed to have the ability to control her own destiny in this other world, even the smallest one... \"Cui Qiao, go and burn a hand stove for Sister Jiu, see how cold your little face is.\" At this time, the door curtain in the west room suddenly opened, and Mrs. Jiang walked out with the support of Cui Ling and Zhou's mother. \"Greetings to mother!\" Sister Jiu quickly stood up and saluted. \"Okay, sit down!\" Mrs. Jiang waved her hand. Na Cuiqiao had already diligently put an exquisite hand stove with a cloisonné enamel flower and bird pattern into Jiu Jie'er's hand, and Jiu Jie'er quickly thanked Jiang again. Mrs. Jiang nodded to her with satisfaction, and then chatted with her for a few words. At this time, the dark blue sky outside the window had dispersed, and the sun appeared. Ms. Jiang glanced outside, a touch of depression slipped over her face. Sister Ninth calmly lowered her eyelids, picked up the tea in her hand and drank it all. Then she turned to Cui Qiao behind her, smiled and whispered, \"Can you please give me another cup, sister? I think the tea here is really delicious!\" \"Miss Ninth...\" Cui Qiao was startled at first, and then smiled, \" To tell you the truth, the mother in the kitchen cooked the red date and ginseng tea today. She added seven or eight kinds of ingredients and cooked it for two hours. \"Really?\" Sister Jiu said with a look of joy and surprise on her face. \"I didn't expect Sister Ninth to be a glutton!\" Mrs. Jiang looked over and said with a smile. \"No, it's because the tea tastes so good...\" Sister Wenjiu said in a low voice with a blush on her face. The people in the room were amused by her embarrassment, and a lot of time passed unknowingly. \"Mom, it's so cold today!\" Only then, accompanied by a crisp voice, did Sister Wen Shi's figure slowly appear at the door...",
